# Patches

- seaview-scheme.patch -- honours $FLTK_SCHEME and X resource colours.
  The desktop file starts it by parsing the FLTK_SCHEME variable. The
  colours are read from ~/.Xresources, for example set something like:

  fltk.background:       #D3D7CF
  fltk.foreground:       #000000
  Text.background:       #ffffff
  Text.selectBackground: #145BA6
  
  Then run:
  
  xrdb -merge ~/.Xresources

- seaview-msa-methods.patch -- adds built-in external alignment methods
  and raises the method limit from 10 to 15:

  | Slot | Method        | Default option (tick box) |
  |------|---------------|---------------------------|
  | 1    | clustalo      |                           |
  | 2    | muscle        |                           |
  | 3    | muscle5       |                           |
  | 4    | mafft --auto  | `--thread -1`             |
  | 5    | mafft-linsi   | `--thread -1`             |
  | 6    | mafft-einsi   | `--thread -1`             |
  | 7    | mafft-ginsi   | `--thread -1`             |
  | 8    | t_coffee      | `-thread 0`               |
  | 9    | kalign        |                           |
  | 10   | prank-io      |                           |

  Slots 1-10 are reserved and cannot be deleted; add your own methods in
  slots 11-15. Methods whose program is not in $PATH are greyed out.
  
  prank-io is a wrapper shipped with the prank port, since PRANK always
  appends `.best.fas` to its output name.

- seaview-interrupt.patch -- Interrupt now stops the aligner's whole
  process group, so helper processes (e.g. T-Coffee workers) are killed
  too, not just the main process.
